{
  "requirement": "`trust_but_verify::outline::OutlineContent` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::NodeContents`, making it usable directly as\n`Domain::NodeContent` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`.\n\nIts `fingerprint()` returns the selected item's retained structural hash and\nscheme under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`.\nIts `format()` returns the selected source text with recognized credentials\nredacted under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.redaction` and\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nBoth operations describe the source snapshot retained by the value.\n`text()` retains the original selected bytes for source inspection.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.outlines.node_contents`**\n1. `OutlineContent` implements `NodeContents`.\n2. `fingerprint()` returns the selected item's retained structural hash and scheme.\n3. `format()` returns the selected text with recognized credentials redacted.\n4. Both operations describe the retained snapshot, so they must not change when the file changes or the handle is dropped.\n5. `text()` keeps the original bytes.\n\n**Tests that cover them**\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]`:\n- It calls `fingerprint()` and `format()` through the imported `NodeContents` trait. That covers obligation 1.\n- It selects the third item, `second`, and asserts `fingerprint().value == structural_hash()` and `fingerprint().scheme == fingerprint_scheme()`. That covers obligation 2.\n- It asserts `format() == \"second\"` and `text() == \"second\"`. That covers obligation 3 for text with no credentials.\n- It saves the fingerprint, drops the file handle and rewrites the file. It then asserts that the fingerprint, `format()` and `text()` of the retained selections are unchanged, and that `from_id` now fails. That covers obligation 4.\n- It re-selects the root from the retained value and asserts its original text. That covers obligation 5.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans]`:\n- The root `text()` equals the original source, and `format()` contains `[REDACTED:GitHub Token]` and not the token. This covers redaction in `format()` and original bytes in `text()`.\n- The line count of `format()` equals the source's line count, which checks that line breaks are preserved.\n- Two sources that differ only in the credential give equal `fingerprint()` values. This matches the redaction requirement's rule that changing only a credential does not change the structural fingerprint.\n- A selected item keeps the token in `text()` but not in `format()`.\n\n**Other tests I looked at**\n\n`#fn[explicit_languages_share_configuration_and_retain_their_scheme]` and `#fn[rust_items_attach_documentation_and_preserve_structural_hashes]` also exercise `fingerprint()`. They check a custom scheme, a changed scheme, and fingerprints that stay the same or change as the source does. They carry no `{test}` reference to this requirement, but the marked tests already cover it. I don't count that as a gap.\n\n**Delegated and non-gaps**\n- The redaction rules themselves and the span-slicing logic in `Redaction::slice` belong to `requirements.sdk.sources.redaction`, which has its own tests. `format()` only passes the selected span to that code.\n- I found no scenario in this requirement's own text that the marked tests would let a violation slip through.",
  "references": "1c6c762f96d1086f3ccea20a1391ce2c8c8311bcd7e386f26abf818136867ca2",
